# App Design Language: [Name]

The visual language for [app name]. Every decision serves [core goal — e.g. "daily usability over visual flair" or "clarity and calm over excitement"].

**North star:** [One sentence. What does great design feel like here? Who is it for?]

---

## 1. Typography

Two fonts: [Serif] for headings, [Sans-serif] for everything else.

Three sizes — pick by role, not pixels:

| Utility | Size | Use for |
|---------|------|---------|
| `text-heading` | 24px | Page titles |
| `text-body` | 16px | Body, buttons, inputs |
| `text-small` | 12px | Captions, badges, helper text |

Two weights: normal (400) for body, semibold (600) for emphasis. Never introduce a third weight without a documented reason.

Never use native Tailwind `text-sm` / `text-lg` for content — use the semantic tokens above so sizes are tunable from one place.

---

## 2. Spacing

Two max-widths:

| Utility | Value | Use for |
|---------|-------|---------|
| `max-w-page` | 1120px | Full-width layouts |
| `max-w-content` | 768px | Focused single-column content |

Standard vertical rhythm: `space-y-6` between top-level sections, `gap-4` between cards.

---

## 3. Radii

Defined as CSS vars; change globally from `:root`.

| Utility | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| `rounded-card` | Cards, dialogs, panels |
| `rounded-button` | Pill buttons |
| `rounded-input` | Inputs, selects |
| `rounded-badge` | Tags, chips |

---

## 4. Elevation

Flat by default. Borders carry depth at rest; shadows activate on interaction.

| Element | Shadow |
|---------|--------|
| Card (resting) | none — border only |
| Card (hover) | baked into `interactive-card` |
| Dialog / popover | `shadow-overlay` |

Never use `hover:shadow-lg` on a card — `interactive-card` owns that recipe.

---

## 5. Colors

All tokens in `:root` / `.dark` in `globals.css`. Never hardcode hex in components.

| Need | Token |
|------|-------|
| Page background | `bg-background` |
| Card background | `bg-card` or `card-surface` utility |
| Primary text | `text-foreground` |
| Secondary text | `text-muted-foreground` |
| Interactive accent | `text-primary` / `bg-primary` |
| Error / destructive | `text-destructive` |

---

## 6. Interactive States

Five utilities handle hover. Never roll bespoke hover in component files.

| Utility | Use for |
|---------|---------|
| `interactive-card` | Clickable cards (border + shadow on hover) |
| `interactive-chip` | Tags, filter chips |
| `interactive-text` | Inline text links |

If `interactive-card` is applied, the element must also declare an explicit `border` at rest — without it the hover border-color has nothing to transition from.

---

## 7. Buttons

Managed by `Button` in `components/ui/button.tsx`. Default to the `gradient` variant for primary CTAs. Do not recreate the CTA gradient inline — use the `cta-gradient` utility.

---

## 8. Cards

Two families:

- **`ContentCard`** — flat info panel, used for settings, forms, copy blocks.
- **`ActionCard`** — interactive surface with `interactive-card` hover, used for navigation and selectable items.

Both use `rounded-card border border-border/60`. Padding is NOT baked in — callers decide.

---

## 9. Loading States

Each component owns its loading branch inline — no global skeleton registry. Use the `Skeleton` primitive (`components/ui/skeleton.tsx`) with `.animate-skeleton-pulse`. Outer shape must match the real component; internal detail doesn't have to.

---

## 10. Animation

Page load: `opacity 0→1`, `y 12→0`, 0.4s ease-out, ~80ms stagger between siblings.

No scroll-triggered reveals, no page transitions, no rotation or bounce animations.

---

## 11. CSS Variables Reference

All defined in `:root` in `globals.css`. Tune from one place.

| Category | Variables |
|----------|-----------|
| Typography | `--text-heading`, `--text-body`, `--text-small` (+ `-lh` pairs) |
| Radii | `--radius-card`, `--radius-button`, `--radius-input`, `--radius-badge` |
| Elevation | `--shadow-card`, `--shadow-elevated`, `--shadow-overlay` |
| Widths | `--width-page`, `--width-content` |
| Gradient | `--gradient-from`, `--gradient-to` |
